-- title:
--   Igusa branch valuation ring at an end of the blow-up
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ be primes with $\ell\neq q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$.
--
--   **The function field.** Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with (`hK`) $K=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. $K$ is generated over $L$ by the image under the coefficient embedding [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the congruence group [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) attached to level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and to the subgroup `levelH (q*ℓ) M'`, which is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   **The base ring.** Let $A$ be a Henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, with $L$ as fraction field, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$; assume $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`). Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}+\dots$ of the modular $j$-function (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`) and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hϖt`). Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` denotes the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A K j` $=j$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7): every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The rigidified local model.** The hypothesis `hArig` (a universally quantified statement over points of the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), summarised here) asserts the following. For every point $z$ of the model at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (pulled back from $\operatorname{Spec} A$) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin = Spec(chartAlgFin A K j)` with `ιFin`-image $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition at $y'$, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, such that: $e$ carries constants from $A$ to the classes of $C(\sigma a)$; every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves the chart algebra; for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ such a $\tau$ induces the identity modulo $y'$; each such $\tau$ inducing the identity modulo $y'$ is realised on $S$ by an automorphism $\theta$ fixing constants, acting on $X_0,X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ through a matrix $M\equiv c\,\gamma$ mod $\mathfrak m_W$ with $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$, with $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; primes of $S$ containing $C(\sigma\varpi)$ with tangent directions $(a_1{:}b_1)$, $(a_2{:}b_2)$ independent modulo $q$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime with tangent direction $(1{:}0)$ an element $a$ of the chart algebra lies in the contracted prime precisely when all Laurent coefficients of $a$ lie in $\mathfrak m_A$; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-expansion with exponents scaled by $q\ell$) lies in the chart algebra and, after subtraction of a suitable $a_0\in A$, corresponds under $e$ to a series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, $e_0\ge1$, whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at all $(a,b)\in W^2$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   A concrete such situation is fixed: a point $z$ with germ $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`-image $z$ (`hy'`), supersingular (`hss'`) and with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`), together with data $W_1,\sigma_1,f_1,u_1,v_1,e_1$ as above (`hu₁`, `hv₁`, `hf₁`, `hσ₁`) and the hypothesis `hW₁` asserting, for these data, exactly the conjunction just described.
--
--   **The blow-up algebras.** Let $J$ be the ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` defined (`hJ`) as the infimum of the ideals obtained, for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra, by pulling back along $\tau$ the contraction to the chart algebra (via the germ map, the completion map and $e_1$) of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ (`hB`) generated over the chart algebra by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$.
--
--   **The reference valuation ring.** Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hR1` states that the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and that $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2` that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) that $W\cap L=A$, that $\mathfrak m_W=(\varpi)$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that the centre of $W$ on the chart algebra is exactly $y$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the centre of $W$ on $B$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho\colon B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the centre of $W$ on $B$, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and equivariant for the level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $W$, through elements $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,c)$ of the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$); that $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the $\tau$-translate of the centre of $W$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in all such translates is divisible by $\varpi$; and that $W$ is $\tau$-stable whenever $y$ is.
--
--   Assume further (`hjK`, `hjC`) that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and (`hm1`, `hmt`) that $m\ge1$ satisfies $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$.
--
--   **Ends and the crossing datum.** Let `ends` be a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised (`hends`) by: $O\in$ `ends` if and only if there are $a\in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ and a maximal ideal $P$ of the $A$-subalgebra $B_a$ generated over the chart algebra by $\{x\in K: xa\in J\}$, such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, every element of $y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit there, and $B\not\subseteq O$. Fix $O\in$ `ends` (`hOmem`) with $O\subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), containing the chart algebra (`hCO`) and $\varpi$ (`hϖO`). Let $c_x,c_y\in O$, $u\in O^\times$ with $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`), and let
--   $$\iota\colon \widehat{O}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\widehat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(X_0X_1-C(\varpi^m)\bigr)$$
--   be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the $\mathfrak m_A$-adic completion $\widehat A$ with parameter $\varpi^m$, together with units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, such that $\iota$ sends the image of $a\in A$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ in $\widehat A$ (`hιc`), and sends $c_x$ to $\gamma_U\cdot$`U` (`hιx`) and $c_y$ to $\gamma_V\cdot$`V` (`hιy`), where `U`, `V` are the two distinguished elements of the crossing model. Finally assume (`hcyW`, `hcxW`) that $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ and $c_x$ does not.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K$ such that:
--
--   1. $O\subseteq W_x$;
--
--   2. `chartAlgFin A K j` $\subseteq W_x$;
--
--   3. for $x\in L$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $W_x$ if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$, i.e. $W_x\cap L=A$;
--
--   4. $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring;
--
--   5. the image of $\varpi$ lies in $W_x$ and generates $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$;
--
--   6. $c_x$ lies in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$;
--
--   7. $c_y$ does not lie in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$;
--
--   8. every $b$ in the chart algebra lying in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ lies in $y$, i.e. the centre of $W_x$ on the chart algebra is contained in $y$;
--
--   9. some $b\in y$ does not lie in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$, i.e. that centre is strictly smaller than $y$.
--
--   Thus $W_x$ is the branch of the blow-up at the end $O$ on which the coordinate $c_x$ vanishes and $c_y$ is invertible, unramified over $A$ with uniformiser $\varpi$, and its centre on the $j$-finite chart is a prime properly contained in the supersingular point $y$.
--
--   This is the existence step for the Igusa branch through an end of the blow-up of the two-chart integral model at a supersingular point: at the node of the crossing model $\widehat O\cong\widehat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$ attached to an end $O$, it produces the discrete valuation ring of $K$ cutting out the branch $U=0$, with prescribed behaviour of the coordinates $c_x,c_y$ and with centre a prime strictly inside the supersingular point. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaValuationSubring_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_igusaValuationSubring_of_mem_ends_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), which assembles the Igusa components from these branches.
